# architect-library — repository

Skill library + custom agent library + Cursor user-global rules. Work in this clone to edit `skills/`, `agents/`, `user-rules/`, `office-tools`, scripts, or docs.

**Install or patch (global default):** after skill, agent, or user-rule changes — or when the user asks (e.g. **install library**) — follow [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) § Install library with **`all cursor` and `all copilot`**. Do not only edit source folders, and do not install only one of those editors unless the user names it. Claude and Codex stay out unless the user asks. A named editor selects only that editor; `all all` selects all four. Cursor details: [architect-library-patch.mdc](architect-library-patch.mdc), [docs/AGENT-SKILL-INSTALL.md](docs/AGENT-SKILL-INSTALL.md).

## Layout

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `skills/` | Skill library source → `~/.cursor/skills/`, `~/.copilot/skills/` |
| `agents/` | Custom agent library source → `~/.cursor/agents/`, `~/.copilot/agents/` |
| `user-rules/cursor/` | Cursor user-global rules source → `~/.cursor/rules/` (not this repo’s `.cursor/rules/`). Includes `review-handoff-reconciliation.mdc`, `response-style.mdc`, `edit-scope.mdc`, `branch-strategy.mdc`, `docs-lookup.mdc`, and `temp-validators.mdc`. |
| `user-rules/copilot/` | Copilot always-on fragments (`response-style.md`, `edit-scope.md`, `branch-strategy.md`, `review-handoff.md`, `docs-lookup.md`, `temp-validators.md`) generated from `user-rules/cursor/` by `scripts/sync_copilot_rules.sh`, then concatenated to `~/.copilot/copilot-instructions.md`. Do not hand-edit. |
| `agents/<name>/INSTRUCTIONS.md` | Shared agent prompt body |
| `agents/<name>/cursor.header.md` | Cursor frontmatter (assembled at install) |
| `agents/<name>/copilot.header.md` | Copilot frontmatter (assembled at install) |
| `agents/<name>/claude.header.md` | Claude Code frontmatter (assembled at install) |
| `skills/excalidraw-diagram/` | Excalidraw → PNG visual QA |
| `skills/word-document/` | DOCX architecture documents |
| `skills/powerpoint-presentation/` | PPTX → **mandatory** layout preview |
| `skills/spreadsheet-document/` | XLSX / spreadsheets; formula recalc via office-tools |
| `skills/pdf-document/` | PDF read/create/merge/forms |
| `skills/github-markdown/` | GitHub Flavored Markdown for READMEs, issues, PRs, discussions, wikis, repo docs |
| `skills/newagentlink/` | One-shot new-agent continuation snapshot (`/tmp/<topic>-newagentlink.md`); Cursor command `cursor.command.md` → `~/.cursor/commands/newagentlink.md` |
| `skills/terraform-commit-review/` | Terraform IaC commit-range review |
| `skills/terraform-apply-assistance/` | Terraform apply fix, scope review, and plan evaluation |
| `skills/notion-mcp-ops/` | Notion MCP CRUD, formatting, fetch-before-write; editor variants for Cursor and Copilot |
| `skills/_shared/` | `architecture-document-principles.md`, `office-tools/` |
| `scripts/install_library.sh` | Install/patch skills, agents, Cursor user-global rules, and the Copilot always-on instruction |
| `scripts/install_deps.sh` | Runtimes only (`all` \| `excalidraw` \| `office` \| `office-system` \| `pdf` \| `node`) |
| `.cursor/rules/` | **Maintainer rules for this repo** — not copied to users |
| `.cursor/skills/absorb-reference-materials/` | **Maintainer skill** — triage `tmp/` ref material (not in `SKILL_BUNDLE`) |
| `tmp/` | Staging for external ref skills/agents — review before import; ignored items stay here |
| `docs/AGENT-SKILL-INSTALL.md` | End-user install guide |
| `docs/MAINTAINING-SKILLS.md` | Maintainer checklist (skills + agents + Cursor user-global rules) |
| `docs/AGENTS.md` | Agent catalog |

Skill behavior: `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` and `skills/<name>/references/`.

## Changing this repo

Do **not** update only scripts or README. When adding or changing a skill, agent, user-global Cursor rule, workflow step, or dependency:

1. Follow [docs/MAINTAINING-SKILLS.md](docs/MAINTAINING-SKILLS.md).
2. **Skill change** → update `skills/*/SKILL.md`, execution rule row, `SKILL_BUNDLE` in `install_library.sh` if new skill, run `bash scripts/install_library.sh skills cursor` and `bash scripts/install_library.sh skills copilot`.
3. **Agent change** → update `agents/<name>/`, [docs/AGENTS.md](docs/AGENTS.md), `AGENT_BUNDLE` in `install_library.sh` if new agent, run `bash scripts/install_library.sh agents cursor` and `bash scripts/install_library.sh agents copilot`.
4. **Cursor user-global rule change** → update `user-rules/cursor/<name>.mdc`, `CURSOR_RULE_BUNDLE` in `install_library.sh` if new, run `bash scripts/sync_copilot_rules.sh`, `bash scripts/sync_codex_rules.sh`, and `bash scripts/sync_claude_rules.sh`, then `bash scripts/install_library.sh rules cursor` and `bash scripts/install_library.sh rules copilot`.
5. **Copilot always-on instruction change** → edit the Cursor source under `user-rules/cursor/`, run `bash scripts/sync_copilot_rules.sh`, `bash scripts/sync_codex_rules.sh`, and `bash scripts/sync_claude_rules.sh` to regenerate `user-rules/copilot/`, `user-rules/codex/`, and `user-rules/claude/`, then `bash scripts/install_library.sh rules copilot`.
6. **Review handoff protocol change** → edit `skills/review-handoff/SKILL.md` (not the trigger rule), run `bash scripts/install_library.sh skills cursor` and `skills copilot`.
7. Always update `README.md`, `docs/AGENT-SKILL-INSTALL.md`, and relevant `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`.

When the user asks to **review or absorb ref material under `tmp/`**, read `.cursor/skills/absorb-reference-materials/SKILL.md` first — ship only high-value skills/agents, harden existing installs, ignore the rest. After absorb: update `README.md` when catalog or layout changes (see `absorb-reference-materials/references/readme-after-absorb.md`).

**Do not:**

- Copy distributable `skills/` into `repo/.cursor/skills/` (exception: maintainer skills under `.cursor/skills/` only).
- Copy `agents/` into `repo/.cursor/agents/` or `repo/.github/agents/` as canonical source.
- Copy `user-rules/cursor/` into `repo/.cursor/rules/` — maintainer rules and user-global rules are different sources. Project-scope install from this clone (any cwd under the clone) skips rules so that copy cannot happen.
- Add agents to `SKILL_BUNDLE`, skills to `AGENT_BUNDLE`, or user-global rules to either of those bundles.

Install bundles for users: run runtime dependencies first, then `bash scripts/install_library.sh all cursor` and `bash scripts/install_library.sh all copilot`. Use `all codex` or `all claude` for an explicitly named editor, and `all all` for an explicit all-editor request. Legacy `both` still excludes Codex.

## Codex installation

When Codex is requested, use `bash scripts/install_library.sh all codex` after
the same runtime setup. Skills go to `~/.agents/skills/`; agents and the managed
`AGENTS.md` block go to `${CODEX_HOME:-$HOME/.codex}`. The six fragments in
`user-rules/codex/` are generated from `user-rules/cursor/` by
`bash scripts/sync_codex_rules.sh`; do not hand-edit them. Run all three sync scripts
with `--check` after user-rule changes. Preserve personal instructions outside
the managed block. Project Codex installs write `.agents/skills/` and
`.codex/agents/` only. See `docs/AGENT-SKILL-INSTALL.md` for conflict handling and
`python3 -m unittest discover -s scripts -p 'test_install_library.py'` for isolated
installer regression checks.

## Claude Code installation

When Claude Code is requested, use `bash scripts/install_library.sh all claude`.
Skills, agents, and rules go to `~/.claude/skills/`, `~/.claude/agents/`, and
`~/.claude/rules/`. The six rule files in `user-rules/claude/` are generated from
`user-rules/cursor/` by `bash scripts/sync_claude_rules.sh`; do not hand-edit them.
The installer never edits `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`. Project Claude installs do not
write `.claude/rules/`.
